Build issue fixed.

### What was wrong
`make` in `.../usart_irq` failed because `examples/rules.mk` only searched a few relative paths for `libopencm3`, and in this workspace the actual library is one level higher than those paths.

### Change made
Updated this file:

- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/rules.mk`

Changed:
```make
LIBPATHS := ./libopencm3 ../../../../libopencm3 ../../../../../libopencm3
```

To:
```make
LIBPATHS := ./libopencm3 ../../../../libopencm3 ../../../../../libopencm3 ../../../../../../libopencm3
```

### Result
Re-running `make` in:
`firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/usart_irq`
now succeeds with no errors.
